/*
 * bitmaps' resources: rc compiles them into bitmaps.res, which links
 * into bitmaps.exe. The language is given as numbers (no header is
 * included): 9, 1 is LANG_ENGLISH, SUBLANG_ENGLISH_US (0x0409).
 *
 * bitmaps.bmp is an 8x8 bitmap of 4 bits per pixel, stored bottom-up,
 * with the 16 VGA colors as its color table (in order: black, maroon,
 * green, olive, navy, purple, teal, silver, gray, red, lime, yellow,
 * blue, fuchsia, aqua, white). The pixel x, y (y counted from the top)
 * holds the index (x + 2 * y) mod 16. It is checked in beside this
 * file; bitmaps.c holds the same table and formula.
 *
 * The bitmap is here twice: by number (300) and by name (F2KBMP).
 */

LANGUAGE 9, 1

300 BITMAP "bitmaps.bmp"
F2KBMP BITMAP "bitmaps.bmp"
